<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
  xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
  package="com.projectstride.stride_health">

  <!--
    Health Connect's client library declares minSdk 26; this plugin and the app
    that hosts it target 24.

    The override is safe here and only here, because absence is a first-class
    answer in this design rather than an error path bolted on afterwards:
    `HealthConnectStepSource.availability()` checks `Build.VERSION.SDK_INT`
    BEFORE the client class is touched and reports SERVICE_MISSING below
    Android 8, which is the same normal, fully-playable state as a phone with
    Health Connect simply not installed. No Health Connect type is loaded on a
    device that cannot support it.

    The alternative was raising the whole application's minSdk to 26 to satisfy
    a dependency the game degrades gracefully without, which would drop
    Android 7 devices for no gain.
  -->
  <uses-sdk tools:overrideLibrary="androidx.health.connect.client" />

  <!--
    Read-only, steps only.

    There is no write permission here and there must not be one: the game reads
    the player's movement and never writes to their health record. There is also
    no history permission - the ledger never needs old data, only what is new
    since the last cursor, and asking for more than that is asking the player to
    grant access the game cannot justify.
  -->
  <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.health.READ_STEPS" />

  <!--
    Package visibility for the Health Connect provider.

    Without this, `HealthConnectClient.getSdkStatus` cannot see the provider on
    Android 11 through 13 and reports it missing on a device that has it
    installed. Absence is a normal state the game stays fully playable through,
    which is exactly why a FALSE absence would be invisible.
  -->
  <queries>
    <package android:name="com.google.android.apps.healthdata" />
  </queries>

  <!--
    Deliberately absent: any background entry point.

    No service, no receiver, no `PassiveMonitoringClient` registration, no
    worker, no boot receiver. S-01A is foreground synchronization only;
    background delivery is S-01B and is blocked on a real persistence
    coordinator. See DECISIONS/0013 and DECISIONS/0014.

    Also deliberately absent: the permission-rationale activity Health Connect
    requires before release. It belongs to the host application, not to this
    plugin, because it is a screen the player sees and this package owns no UI.
  -->
</manifest>
